WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.010
Whether it's music, sports, or film, if there's
something people love, you can count on fans

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:07.510
crossing the line into full blown crazy.

00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:11.870
And comic book fans are no exception, especially
since Marvel movies began dominating at the

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:12.870
box office.

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:17.230
So grab your Mjolnir and hold on tight, because
here's a look at a few Marvel fans who took

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:19.210
things too far.

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:21.160
It ain't easy bein' green

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:26.580
In 2012, a 35-year-old Brazilian man named
Paulo Henrique dos Santos painted himself

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:29.130
green and dressed as the Hulk for a running
event.

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:33.750
Unfortunately, the paint turned out to be
super heavy duty stuff used on ballistic missiles

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:34.960
and nuclear submarines.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:36.000
And whattya know?

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.480
It wouldn't wash off.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:40.960
Even after 20 baths, Santos remained as green
as the Hulk.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:45.370
It eventually took a crowd of friends 24 hours
of scrubbing to finally get the green paint

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:47.340
out of Santos' skin.

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:49.530
No wonder the Hulk is always angry!

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:52.000
(Roars)

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.100
"What the hell?"

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:56.129
The best there is at what he does

00:00:56.129 --> 00:01:01.750
In October 2017, during an Australian comic
convention, a 28-year-old man dressed as Wolverine

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:05.360
was arrested for allegedly playing his part
a little too well.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:09.369
Around 2 a.m., after being kicked out of a
pub on Sydney's King's St., the Wolverine

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:13.799
fan allegedly attacked two men, injuring one
and knocking the other unconscious.

00:01:13.799 --> 00:01:18.369
Both victims were brought to the hospital
while the man dressed as Wolverine was arrested.

00:01:18.369 --> 00:01:22.229
It was not revealed if the dispute began over
an underground cage match or if either of

00:01:22.229 --> 00:01:26.240
the alleged victims had called the wanna-be
Wolverine a "dirty mutie" before hostilities

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:27.579
broke out.

00:01:27.579 --> 00:01:29.759
Spider-Man: hero or menace?

00:01:29.759 --> 00:01:30.820
What's better than one Spider-Man?

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:33.680
Well, the answer is lots of Spider-Men, right?

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:38.930
"Earlier today tragedy striking the musical,
Spider-Man Too: 2 Many Spider-Men.

00:01:38.930 --> 00:01:43.350
The show, billed as the most Spider-Men ever
assembled on one stage."

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:48.140
Well, if J. Jonah Jameson were real, the crimes
allegedly perpetrated by people dressed as

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:50.009
Spider-Man would've made him feel pretty vindicated.

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:55.760
For instance, a robber dressed as Spider-Man
allegedly held up an HSBC Bank in the Bronx

00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:00.890
in April of 2017 as part of a Spidey crime
spree involving a number of attempted thefts.

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:02.960
And that's not the first time.

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:05.962
From NYC, to Frederick, Maryland, to sunny
St. Cloud, Florida, Spider-Man seems to be

00:02:05.962 --> 00:02:08.800
the hero costume of choice for would-be criminals.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:13.270
But there are heroic Spider-Men as well, such
as the Birmingham, England Spidey who donned

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:14.880
the suit to feed the homeless.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:19.640
And then there's Kevin Gordon-Prior, who reportedly
broke up a brawl between around 30 or 40 people

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:21.570
in England while dressed as Spidey.

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:25.160
And it wasn't the first time he made headlines
for saving the day as Spider-Man, either.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:28.330
Hey, with no power comes great responsibility.

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:29.460
The King of Pop Art

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:35.400
At the 2009 San Diego Comic Con, shortly after
Michael Jackson's death, Stan Lee opened up

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:38.580
about the King of Pop's interest in Marvel
and Spider-Man.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:42.490
Lee claimed he and Jackson had sat down once
to discuss the possibility of pooling their

00:02:42.490 --> 00:02:47.570
resources to buy Marvel Comics, with at least
part of Jackson's incentive being to get control

00:02:47.570 --> 00:02:49.580
over film portrayals of Spider-Man.

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:50.580
Lee said,

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:53.480
"I'm not sure whether he just wanted to produce
it or wanted to play the role.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:55.430
Our conversation never got that far along."

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:59.910
Jackson playing Spidey may sound far-fetched,
but it apparently wasn't the only superhero

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:05.281
he had his eye on, as X-Men screenwriter David
Hayter revealed in 2017 that Michael Jackson

00:03:05.281 --> 00:03:09.110
wanted the film role of X-Men founder Professor
X.

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:10.110
Seeing Red

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:14.850
When you think of the most extreme, hardcore
fans and the subjects of their obsession,

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:18.660
you probably wouldn't choose Captain America
bad guy The Red Skull as the most obvious

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:20.400
subject of such intense passion.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:25.560
But Venezuela's Henry Rodriguez has taken
fan obsession to a whole new level, even undergoing

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:28.660
facial reconstruction to look more like the
arch villain.

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:33.130
His transformation includes facial and eye
tattoos, cutting off his nose, and subdermal

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:35.140
implants in his face and brow.

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:36.950
And did we mention he CUT OFF HIS NOSE?!

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:42.940
Unfortunately, all that face-altering has
him looking less like the Red Skull and more

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:44.660
like Wrex from Mass Effect.

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:56.600
Thanks for watching!

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:59.480
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:03:59.490 --> 00:04:01.780
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

